<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aegĭum</span></b> , or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aegĭon</span></b> , ii, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Achaia</i>,
				<i>one of the twelve Achœan cities</i>,
				<i>situated on the river Selinus</i>, now <i>Vostitza</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 5,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 5, 6, § 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lucr. 6,
			585</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 30</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aegĭenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Achaia</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
			30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 4, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aegĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>pertaining to
				Ægium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis,</span>”
				<i>a kind of vine</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 3, 4, § 42</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
